\n\n\n### ard-bot-albertcbrown[bot] at 2026-11-24T17:58:24Z\n\n<!-- ard:closeout job=01M87B9GPASZXM77BSCDN277GZ attempt=1 -->\n**ard · triage:engineer · done**\n\nAdds a patch-id comparison to the shared head-cover check so a path changed by both the PR and main stays covered when the PR's own patch to it is unchanged after a clean update-branch merge. It wires the rule into the merger's review gate and approval check, logs the covered paths, and updates the proposal. The plan has five steps with real-repo tests for each acceptance case. Size M, risk medium because it loosens a security-relevant gate.\n\n## Open issues\n- The old merge base is derived from the first update-branch merge's second parent, since main's tip at review time is not recorded. A maintainer may want to confirm that choice.\n- The cover check's git interface widens, so test fakes in the merger and reviewer packages need updating.\n\nOutput: [.ard/332/triage-engineer.md](https://github.com/albertcbrown/ard/blob/c5afedcafa998f9f3f07ce20bae0fbb62e932638/.ard/332/triage-engineer.md) · log [.ard/332/logs/triage-engineer-20261124T175738.020Z.log](https://github.com/albertcbrown/ard/blob/c5afedcafa998f9f3f07ce20bae0fbb62e932638/.ard/332/logs/triage-engineer-20261124T175738.020Z.log) · job `01M87B9GPASZXM77BSCDN277GZ` · attempt 1\n\n\n# Plan for #332\n\n## Implementation\n\n### Steps\n1. `internal/gitx/inspect.go` (new methods on `*Git`, same style as `MergeBase`, using `g.run` with `--git-dir=gitDirOf(repoDir)`):\n   - `Parents(ctx, repoDir, rev string) ([]string, error)`: `git rev-list --parents -n 1 <rev>`, returns the parent SHAs.\n   - `PatchID(ctx, repoDir, from, to, path string) (string, error)`: run `git diff --no-ext-diff --no-textconv --no-renames <from> <to> -- <path>` (use the `GIT_ATTR_SOURCE=emptyTree` and `GIT_OPTIONAL_LOCKS=0` env that `CodeChanged` uses), pipe it via the `stdin` argument of `g.run` into `git patch-id --stable`, and return the first field. An empty diff or empty output 