{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChNE4ZX6ETycvkydXhFXN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The merger now treats a path that both the PR and main changed as still covered when the PR's own patch to it is unchanged after an update-branch merge. `go test ./...` passes, including the new tests.\n\n- **Rule:** the merger's review gate and the protected-path approval check use the new `CoversDetail` in `internal/prgate/prgate.go`. It compares the stable patch id of the PR's diff to each shared path before and after the update. It only applies when the head reaches the reviewed commit through two-parent merges along first parents. Any git error fails closed.\n- **Unchanged callers:** `Covers` keeps its signature and the plain rule. Mark-ready and reviewfix landing therefore behave as before.\n- **Logging:** the merger logs the paths covered this way as `merge.cover_patch_equal`.\n- **Old merge base:** it is taken from the first update merge's second parent, as the plan says. Main's tip at review time isn't recorded, so a maintainer may want to confirm that choice.\n- **Tests:** real-repo tests cover each acceptance case:\n  - a clean merge, including a chain of merges, stays covered;\n  - a later PR commit, a hand edit in the merge, and a conflict-resolution stand-in are not covered;\n  - git errors return the error and are not covered.\n\n  `gitx` has tests for `PatchID` and `Parents`.\n- **Not done:** there is no merger-level test of the `merge.cover_patch_equal` log, since the rule itself is tested in prgate. `make docs-check` couldn't run because mkdocs isn't installed here. I updated the merger section of `docs/proposal.md` to describe the rule.\n\nThe report is in `.ard/332/worker-engineer.md`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":790,"cache_read_input_tokens":39100,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5